[{:adr/dual-actuation-8790 "matching nursing/8710's, laundry/9601's and holdco/6420's dual-actuation-on-one-entity precedent, this blueprint's own business-model.md Offer lists 'care-plan proposal' and 'incident-response proposal' as two SEPARATE items, and the README/business-model.md/operator-guide.md consistently name BOTH acts together ('finalizing a care plan or incident response') -- two conceptually distinct real-world acts (proactive planning vs. reactive incident handling), so this build uses the two-member high-stakes set #{:actuation/finalize-care-plan :actuation/finalize-incident-response}, each with its own history collection, sequence counter and dedicated double-actuation-guard boolean", :adr/related ["2607071250-cloud-itonami-brokerage-6612-coverage" "2607071320-cloud-itonami-credit-6492-coverage" "2607071351-cloud-itonami-accounting-6920-coverage" "2607071618-cloud-itonami-marketadmin-6611-coverage" "2607071640-cloud-itonami-testlab-7120-coverage" "2607071654-cloud-itonami-clinic-8620-coverage" "2607071717-cloud-itonami-registrar-8530-coverage" "2607071732-cloud-itonami-wagering-9200-coverage" "2607071752-cloud-itonami-veterinary-7500-coverage" "2607071819-cloud-itonami-funeral-9603-coverage" "2607071849-cloud-itonami-repairshop-9521-coverage" "2607071922-cloud-itonami-parksafety-9321-coverage" "2607072715-cloud-itonami-eldercare-8730-coverage" "2607072730-cloud-itonami-museum-9102-coverage" "2607072745-cloud-itonami-conservation-9103-coverage" "2607072800-cloud-itonami-salon-9602-coverage" "2607072815-cloud-itonami-entertainment-9000-coverage" "2607072830-cloud-itonami-casework-8890-coverage" "2607072845-cloud-itonami-hospital-8610-coverage" "2607072900-cloud-itonami-facility-9311-coverage" "2607072915-cloud-itonami-school-8510-coverage" "2607080100-cloud-itonami-association-9412-coverage" "2607080200-cloud-itonami-leasing-6491-coverage" "2607080300-cloud-itonami-behavioral-8720-coverage" "2607080400-cloud-itonami-secondary-8521-coverage" "2607080500-cloud-itonami-card-6619-coverage" "2607080600-cloud-itonami-water-3600-coverage" "2607080700-cloud-itonami-telecom-6190-coverage" "2607080800-cloud-itonami-aerospace-3030-coverage" "2607080900-cloud-itonami-recovery-3830-coverage" "2607081000-cloud-itonami-consulting-7020-coverage" "2607081100-cloud-itonami-union-9420-coverage" "2607081200-cloud-itonami-congregation-9491-coverage" "2607081300-cloud-itonami-fab-2610-coverage" "2607081400-cloud-itonami-energy-3512-coverage" "2607081500-cloud-itonami-care-8810-coverage" "2607081600-cloud-itonami-navigator-8691-coverage" "2607081700-cloud-itonami-learning-8569-coverage" "2607081800-cloud-itonami-banking-6419-coverage" "2607081900-cloud-itonami-advertising-7310-coverage" "2607082100-cloud-itonami-polling-7320-coverage" "2607082200-cloud-itonami-research-7210-coverage" "2607082300-cloud-itonami-design-7410-coverage" "2607082600-cloud-itonami-nursing-8710-coverage" "2607082800-cloud-itonami-sports-8541-coverage" "2607082900-cloud-itonami-alliedhealth-8690-coverage" "2607083000-cloud-itonami-laundry-9601-coverage" "2607083300-cloud-itonami-holdco-6420-coverage" "2607083500-cloud-itonami-photo-7420-coverage" "2607083600-cloud-itonami-personalservice-9609-coverage" "2607083800-cloud-itonami-edsupport-8550-coverage" "2607084000-cloud-itonami-headoffice-7010-coverage" "2607032000-cloud-itonami-insurance-real-estate-coverage" "cloud-itonami-isic-6511/6512/6621/6622/6629/6520/6530/6820/6612/6492/6920/6611/7120/8620/8530/9200/7500/9603/9521/9321/8730/9102/9103/9602/9000/8890/8610/9311/8510/9412/6491/8720/8521/6619/3600/6190/3030/3830/7020/9420/9491/2610/3512/8810/8691/8569/6419/7310/7320/7210/7410/8710/8541/8690/9601/6420/7420/9609/8550/7010 ADR-0001s" "langgraph ADR-0001"], :adr/distinctive-check-8790 "mandatory-reporting-obligation-unresolved-violations is a GENUINELY NEW concept (grep-verified absent as a dedicated CHECK FUNCTION across every prior sibling), the 51st distinct application of the unconditional-evaluation discipline overall (casualty.governor/sanctions-violations's original fix; most recently edsupport.governor/background-check-not-cleared-violations at 50th), grounded in real child-welfare mandatory-reporting law: US CAPTA (42 U.S.C. section 5106g), Japan's Child Abuse Prevention Act Article 6, and Germany's SGB VIII section 8a", :adr/status :accepted, :adr/id "2607084300", :adr/lesson-applied-proactively-8790 "tested via :safeguarding/screen and :background-check/screen directly from the start (not via an actuation op against an unscreened resident), applying parksafety's ADR-2607071922 Decision 5 / eldercare's, museum's, conservation's, salon's, entertainment's, casework's, hospital's, facility's, school's, association's, leasing's, behavioral's, secondary's, card's, water's, telecom's, aerospace's, recovery's, consulting's, union's, congregation's, fab's, energy's, care's, navigator's, learning's, banking's, advertising's, polling's, research's, design's, nursing's, sports's, alliedhealth's, laundry's, holdco's, photo's, personalservice's, edsupport's and headoffice's ADR-0001 lesson PROACTIVELY for a fortieth consecutive vertical", :adr/fleet-maturity-before "{:implemented 66, :blueprint 18, :spec 546, :total 643}", :adr/next-vertical-selection-unconstrained true, :adr/pattern-8790 "sealed ResidentialOps-LLM + independent Residential Care Governor + append-only audit ledger, modeled closely on all sixty-six prior actors; FIFTY-THIRD build outside ADR-2607032000's original insurance/real-estate batch (after 6612, 6492, 6920, 6611, 7120, 8620, 8530, 9200, 7500, 9603, 9521, 9321, 8730, 9102, 9103, 9602, 9000, 8890, 8610, 9311, 8510, 9412, 6491, 8720, 8521, 6619, 3600, 6190, 3030, 3830, 7020, 9420, 9491, 2610, 3512, 8810, 8691, 8569, 6419, 7310, 7320, 7210, 7410, 8710, 8541, 8690, 9601, 6420, 7420, 9609, 8550, 7010)", :adr/two-screening-ops-8790 "this build has TWO screening ops (:safeguarding/screen and :background-check/screen) because it introduces two genuinely independent unconditional-evaluation concerns (a NEW mandatory-reporting concept and an honestly-reused background-check concept), each gated by its own dedicated HARD check, following the 'screen the screening op directly' discipline for both -- matching edsupport/8550's own two-screening-op precedent", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/test-status-8790 "35 tests / 184 assertions, lint clean, demo verified end-to-end (one clean dual-actuation lifecycle plus four HARD-hold cases); kotoba-lang/industry's own full test suite re-run with the local-root technology override before committing -- 7 tests / 115 assertions, all green, no pre-existing fixture referenced ISIC \"8790\"", :adr/body "# ADR-2607084300: `cloud-itonami-isic-8790` (other residential care activities) deepened to `:implemented`\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted.\n\n## Related\n\n- ADR-2607032000 (original insurance/real-estate batch)\n- ADR-2607083600 (`cloud-itonami-isic-9609`, other personal service activities n.e.c.)\n- ADR-2607083800 (`cloud-itonami-isic-8550`, educational support activities)\n- ADR-2607084000 (`cloud-itonami-isic-7010`, activities of head offices)\n- `cloud-itonami-isic-8790/docs/adr/0001-architecture.md` (child-repo architecture ADR)\n- `langgraph` ADR-0001 (StateGraph actor pattern)\n\n## Context\n\n`cloud-itonami-isic-8790` publishes an OSS business blueprint for\nother residential care activities not elsewhere classified: children's\nhomes, orphanages, residential care for the homeless and similar\nvulnerable-population residential settings. Like every prior vertical\nin this fleet, the blueprint text alone is not an implementation —\nthis ADR records the governed-actor build that promotes `cloud-\nitonami-isic-8790` from `:blueprint` to `:implemented` in the\n`kotoba-lang/industry` registry, the fifty-third vertical built\noutside ADR-2607032000's original insurance/real-estate batch.\n\n## Problem\n\n1. `cloud-itonami-isic-8790`'s blueprint described a real-world\n   residential-care operating model (resident intake, care-plan\n   verification, safeguarding/background-check screening, care-plan\n   and incident-response finalization) but had no governed-actor\n   implementation: no Store, no Governor, no rollout phasing, no\n   tests.\n2. The blueprint's own text consistently names TWO real-world acts\n   together (\"finalizing a care plan or incident response\"), and the\n   business-model.md's own Offer lists them as two separate items —\n   this build needed to resolve whether that is one conceptual act or\n   two distinct actuations.\n3. Residential care for vulnerable populations (children, homeless\n   individuals) carries a genuine, real-world compliance concern\n   distinct from every prior sibling: mandatory-reporting law\n   requires unresolved child-abuse/neglect (or comparable vulnerable-\n   adult) concerns to be reported before a care plan or incident\n   response can be finalized — no dedicated check for this concept\n   exists anywhere else in this fleet, despite the fleet already\n   having many unconditional-evaluation groundings for other concerns.\n4. This fleet already has a \"background check not cleared\" concept\n   (`school`/8510, reused by `sports`/8541, `personalservice`/9609\n   and `edsupport`/8550) — this build's own background-check\n   screening needed to honestly characterize its own reuse rather\n   than overclaim novelty.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Dual-actuation-on-one-entity shape.** Matching `nursing`/8710's,\n   `laundry`/9601's and `holdco`/6420's precedent — the blueprint's\n   Offer lists \"care-plan proposal\" and \"incident-response proposal\"\n   as two SEPARATE items, and the two acts are conceptually distinct\n   (a proactive planning act vs. a reactive incident-handling act),\n   unlike `sports`/8541's genuinely ambiguous either/or phrasing.\n   `high-stakes` is the two-member set `#{:actuation/finalize-care-\n   plan :actuation/finalize-incident-response}`, each with its own\n   history collection, sequence counter and dedicated double-\n   actuation-guard boolean.\n2. **Entity and op shape.** Primary entity `resident`. Six ops:\n   `:resident/intake`, `:careplan/verify`, `:safeguarding/screen`,\n   `:background-check/screen`, `:actuation/finalize-care-plan`\n   (high-stakes), `:actuation/finalize-incident-response`\n   (high-stakes).\n3. **`mandatory-reporting-obligation-unresolved-violations` — the\n   51st unconditional-evaluation grounding, a genuinely new concept.**\n   Grep-verified absent as a dedicated CHECK FUNCTION across every\n   prior sibling. Grounded in US CAPTA (42 U.S.C. §5106g), Japan's\n   Child Abuse Prevention Act Article 6, and Germany's SGB VIII §8a.\n   Gates `:safeguarding/screen` and both actuations.\n4. **`background-check-not-cleared-violations` — an honest FIFTH\n   literal reuse, not claimed as new.** `school.governor` established\n   this concept first; `sports.governor` reused it literally as the\n   second instance; `personalservice.governor` as the third;\n   `edsupport.governor` as the fourth; this build's reuse is the\n   fifth, the 52nd distinct application of the unconditional-\n   evaluation discipline overall. Gates `:background-check/screen`\n   and both actuations.\n5. **TWO dedicated double-actuation-guard booleans.** `:care-plan-\n   finalized?` and `:incident-response-finalized?`, never a single\n   `:status` value, each with its own history/sequence.\n6. **Store protocol, MemStore + DatomicStore parity**, proven via\n   `test/residential/store_contract_test.clj`. The per-entity\n   accessor is safely named `resident` directly.\n7. **Phase 0→3 rollout** — Phase 3's `:auto` set is `{:resident/\n   intake}` only; both actuations are permanently excluded from every\n   phase's `:auto` set.\n8. **No bespoke domain capability lib** — this blueprint's own\n   `:itonami.blueprint/required-technologies` names no domain-\n   specific capability beyond the generic stack.\n9. **Mock + LLM advisor pair** — `mock-advisor` default everywhere,\n   `llm-advisor` with a defensive EDN-proposal parser.\n10. **No `blueprint.edn` field-sync fixes needed** — the `isic-`\n    prefixed `:id` and `:required-technologies`/`:optional-\n    technologies` already matched the `kotoba-lang/industry` registry\n    exactly; only the `:maturity` field itself needed adding.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Sixty-seventh actor in this fleet (66 implemented before this\n  build).\n- Establishes a genuinely NEW unconditional-evaluation-screening\n  concept (mandatory-reporting-obligation-unresolved), grep-verified\n  absent from every prior sibling before the claim was finalized.\n- Documents an honest FIFTH literal reuse of the background-check-\n  not-cleared concept (school 1st, sports 2nd, personalservice 3rd,\n  edsupport 4th, residential 5th), not claimed as new.\n- Confirms the dual-actuation-on-one-entity shape generalizes to a\n  4th instance in this fleet (nursing, laundry, holdco, residential).\n- `MemStore` ‖ `DatomicStore` parity is proven by `test/residential/\n  store_contract_test.clj`.\n- Fleet maturity: `:implemented` 66 → 67, `:blueprint` 18 → 17,\n  `:spec` 546 unchanged, total 643.\n- Test status: 35 tests / 184 assertions, lint clean, demo verified\n  end-to-end.\n- `kotoba-lang/industry`'s full test suite re-run with the local-root\n  `technology` override before committing — 7 tests / 115 assertions,\n  all green, no pre-existing fixture referenced ISIC \"8790\".\n- This build's `deps.edn` used the CURRENT `kotoba-lang/langgraph`/\n  `langchain` coordinates from the start (see `holdco`/6420's own\n  ADR-0001 for the upstream-rename context this build inherited).\n- Next vertical selection remains unconstrained under the standing\n  authorization.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|---|---|\n| Treating \"care plan or incident response\" as one conceptual act (following `sports`/8541's either/or precedent) | Unlike `sports`/8541's genuinely ambiguous phrasing, this blueprint's Offer section lists the two acts as SEPARATE line items, and they are conceptually distinct (proactive planning vs. reactive incident handling) — matching `nursing`/8710's own resolution of a nearly identical pattern |\n| Reusing `nursing`/8710's `credential-not-current` concept instead of a new mandatory-reporting concept | This blueprint's population (children/vulnerable residents) and domain concern (safeguarding/abuse reporting, not staff credentialing) call for a distinct, dedicated check grounded in real child-welfare law |\n| A single combined screening op covering both distinctive concerns | The two concerns are independently groundable in different real-world regulatory regimes; two separate dedicated ops more precisely match the \"screen the screening op directly\" discipline |\n\n## References\n\n- `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-8790/docs/adr/0001-architecture.md`\n- `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-8790/README.edn`\n- `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-8790/docs/business-model.md`\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/industry/resources/kotoba/industry/registry.edn` (entry `\"8790\"`)", :adr/fleet-maturity-after "{:implemented 67, :blueprint 17, :spec 546, :total 643}", :adr/honest-reuse-check-8790 "background-check-not-cleared-violations is an honest FIFTH literal reuse of school.governor's concept (established FIRST), sports.governor's (SECOND), personalservice.governor's (THIRD) and edsupport.governor's (FOURTH) -- NOT claimed as new, the 52nd distinct application of the unconditional-evaluation discipline overall", :adr/no-bespoke-capability-lib-8790 "this blueprint's own :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies names no domain-specific capability beyond the generic robotics/identity/forms/dmn/bpmn/audit-ledger stack -- there was no capability-lib decision to make at all", :adr/date "2026-07-08", :adr/blueprint-already-correct-8790 "this repo's blueprint.edn already had the correct isic- prefixed :id and correctly populated :required-technologies/:optional-technologies matching the kotoba-lang/industry registry's own entry for \"8790\" exactly -- only the :maturity field itself needed adding", :adr/scope-note "this is a NEW ADR because ISIC 8790 (other residential care activities) contributes a genuinely new check concept (mandatory-reporting-obligation-unresolved?) and confirms the dual-actuation-on-one-entity shape generalizes to a 4th instance, warranting its own record per this fleet's standing per-vertical-ADR convention", :db/id -1, :adr/deps-edn-current-coordinates-from-start-8790 "this build's deps.edn used the CURRENT io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph + langchain coordinates and :local/root paths from the very start, inheriting the fix holdco/6420's build discovered and documented -- see holdco/6420's own ADR-0001 for the full upstream-rename context (a repo transfer + rename, internal namespaces unchanged)", :adr/deepened-to-implemented "cloud-itonami-isic-8790", :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isic-8790 (other residential care activities) deepened to :implemented -- fifty-third vertical outside the original batch", :adr/source-format "edn"}]